@startuml seq-illustrate
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 210
skinparam wrapWidth 190
skinparam shadowing false
title Illustrating a chapter\n(spec: chat-node.component.spec.ts · node-action-state.spec.ts · orchestration.spec.ts)
' Aliases match docs/specs/component-map.puml.

actor User
participant "CMP_NODE\nChatNodeComponent\n(the card)" as NODE
participant "CMP_NODE_ACTIONS\nIllustrationController" as ILL
participant "CMP_NODE_ACTIONS\nNodeActionState" as ACT
participant "DLG_IMAGE\nIllustrateDialogService" as DLG
participant "ORCH_RUNNER\nLlmUseCaseRunner" as RUN
participant "ORCH_CORE\nLlmPostprocessorService" as POST
participant "SVC_CHAT\nChatService (facade)" as SVC
participant "PORT\nChatApiPort" as API

== 1. The card collects what only it can see ==
User -> NODE : clicks Illustrate (optionally with a marked text)
NODE -> NODE : captureMarkedSceneText()\n(editor textarea selection, else DOM selection\ninside #readContent)
NODE -> ILL : illustrate({ pressed, markedSceneText,\n  onActivated })
note right of NODE
  The controller never touches viewChild refs: everything DOM-bound
  is passed per call. A direction node delegates to the ASSISTANT
  chapter that answers it — the picture attaches to that chapter.
end note

== 2. Guards: one action at a time ==
ILL -> ACT : idle?
note right of ACT
  node-action-state.spec: begin(kind) is refused while ANY action runs,
  end() clears both flags. A second send / illustrate / version write
  on the same card would otherwise race.
end note
ILL -> ILL : resolve the image-create task model\n(fallback: first enabled image-capable model)
ILL -> DLG : open({ modelId, providerId, sceneText? })
DLG --> ILL : IllustrateOptions | null
note right of DLG
  null = cancelled ⇒ nothing runs (no busy state, no LLM call).
  The use case is DERIVED from the options by pickUsecase().
end note

== 3. Run the use case ==
ILL -> SVC : beginChatOperation(chatId, 'illustrate')
ILL -> ACT : begin('image')
alt storyboard use case (several pictures)
  ILL -> SVC : isIllustrating = true  (surfaces the toolbar Stop)
  note right of ILL
    onImages(scenes) attaches each finished picture to the chapter
    IMMEDIATELY, serialized: every write versions the node, so the
    next write must target the id the previous write returned.
  end note
end
ILL -> RUN : run({ chat, node: chapter, usecase, vars })
RUN --> ILL : EvalSlots (text · images · storyboard)
ILL -> ACT : end()  (finally)
ILL -> SVC : endChatOperation(chatId)

== 4. Place the result on the chapter ==
ILL -> POST : plan(result, build)
POST --> ILL : placement plan (illustration-N + prompt-N / refused-prompt-N)
alt storyboard
  ILL -> SVC : editAssistant(base attachments + final plan)
  note right of ILL
    The final plan REPLACES the interim progressive writes (they are a
    superset of the start state), so pictures never duplicate.
  end note
else single picture
  ILL -> POST : apply(plan, build)
  POST -> SVC : editAssistant(...)
end
SVC -> API : editAssistant(...)  → new node version
API --> SVC : saved node
ILL -> NODE : onActivated(saved.id)  → activate.emit
note right of ILL
  Refused path: no image ⇒ the card shows the model's own refusal
  reason (never a silent success). Partial storyboard ⇒ an info toast
  with "got N of M", the rendered pictures are kept.
end note

== 5. Adapting a recorded prompt ==
User -> NODE : opens a prompt record, edits it, presses Re-render
NODE -> ILL : rerenderPrompt(node, record, draftPrompt\n, { onActivated })
ILL -> ACT : idle? + begin('image')
ILL -> RUN : run(usecase: 'image-generation',\n  vars: { promptText, count: 1 })
RUN --> ILL : scenes
ILL -> ILL : placeRerenderResult(generated, rest,\n  preferredScene)
note right of ILL
  The adapted result takes the RECORDED scene number when it is free and
  drops the paired illustration of that scene, so a re-render REPLACES
  the picture instead of adding a second one. A re-refused attempt
  stays a refused-prompt record (never demoted to a success prompt).
end note
ILL -> SVC : editAssistant(merged attachments)
SVC -> API : editAssistant(...)
API --> SVC : saved node (new version)
ILL -> ACT : end()  (finally)
ILL -> NODE : onActivated(saved.id)

@enduml
